"prose": [
{
"from": 458,
"to": 468,
"text": "The block runs in this order: - **Phase A:** the formatter, the linter, the agent crate's cases, the state crate's cases, the root bin's cases. - **Phase B:** the two filtered control entries. - **Phase C:** the rig library cases, then the rehearsal pair. - **Phase D:**   - the unit, integration and E2E layers;   - the boot smoke (`src/cmd/run.rs` is the boot path; the harness default home keeps the key off);   - then the round: PATH's version, the census, the build with its hash, the live stamps sha, the runtime dir, then     `AV`;   - then the census keyed `operator` and the sha read after. - **Phase E:** the operator pass."
},
{
"from": 470,
"to": 474,
"text": "What is not run, and why: - No mutation run (`inputs#I1` item 8). - No release check entry: CI's `release` job runs `scripts/release-check.sh` on the push, and no new binary or feature   is added. - The fake agent's `fake-args` is test-only code in a `fake-agent` binary."
},
{
"from": 476,
"to": 479,
"text": "Bounds and homes: every test start runs under its test-owned home and user home (tests S1). The live start runs under the rig's private scratch at `/tmp/viola-rig-<uid>/`, and the rig's `--deadline` bounds it under the entry's `timeout`. `AV` is ledgered in `.andromeda/cache/chunks/2026-11-20-a-new-cli-version-stamped-automatically/evidence/auto-starts.ndjson`. `--cap` is the running total of base lines in that one file (`inputs#I1` item 5)."
},
{
"from": 481,
"to": 489,
"text": "**The live entry's `AV` atoms** (`av-key:`, `auto-verify-pairs:`, `stamp-ids:`, `verdict-match:`, `snapshot:`) come from the print site step 19 writes. Their must-pass reading is the rehearsal entry (step 22), fired over the fake agent after the build and before the round. It reads them green on a stamping fake and `stamp-verdict: unverified` on its red sibling. The standing words come from `crates/viola-e2e/src/rig/mod.rs`: - `census`, `credentials` and `scratch` at :695-697; - `user-config` at :713; - `record-left` at :667; - `viola-build` at :1163; - `keys` at :1246."
},
{
"from": 491,
"to": 492,
"text": "The live leg's non-priming probe is the `path-cli:` round entry, listed first. The census, the build, the sha read and the runtime-dir read follow it; none of them primes anything."
},
{
"from": 494,
"to": 498,
"text": "**The remove-the-guard controls** are implement's one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries (validation.md check 4 (6)). - Each fires on an entry filtered to its own case alone (`inputs#I1` item 6). - Each reads «holds» only when its named case ran and FAILED with no TIMEOUT line. Its record lists every case that   failed in the removed run."
},
{
"from": 500,
"to": 506,
"text": "| | `attempted-arm` | `verify-lock` | |---|---|---| | **File** | `src/run/auto_verify.rs` | `src/run/auto_verify.rs` | | **The edit removes** | `decide`'s `EarlierRed` arm, so an `Attempted` unverified entry reads `Verify` (implement quotes the exact text in the control record) | the `Ok(None)` arm of the lock's match, so a held lock goes on to verify as if taken (implement quotes the exact text) | | **Case** | `verify_window_run_whose_verify_goes_red_records_it_and_the_next_start_runs_none` (start 2 counts one `auto-verify` line, not zero) | `verify_window_two_starts_at_once_run_one_verify` (B runs a verify: two `auto-verify` starts) | | **Fired on** | the entry filtered to that case, `--timeout 600` | the entry filtered to that case, `--timeout 600` | | **A timeout reads as** | not held: the case must FAIL | not held |"
}
],
